A||||5||Jim's87GT||F&N air filters?  Good?||||14||
Z||000000||Jim's87GT||03-15-2000||04:48 PM||||A friend is VERY fond of F&N air filters, are they worthwhile in your opinion?  My friend seems to feel that the roughly $40 cost (from PEP BOYS) is more than woth the price.||||reg||14
Z||000001||william_thorniii||03-15-2000||04:55 PM||||Jim,<P>You have done wonder's with your car.  I feel good when I can just keep mine running, you have managed to teach it how to communicate.  WOW!... (for those of you lost, I found some humor in the screen name Jim's87GT.  To me it sounded like it was the screen name not of Jim, but of his Fiero in stead.)<P>Please don't take that the wrong way Jim, just trying to welcome you to the Forum in my own special way.  <P>Now on to the subject at hand...  K & N Filters are a great filter.  They do end up being worth the $ (imho) because they are re-useable.  The performance increase is mostly due to the power of suggestion and hype.  They do help free up some air though.  The bottom line is if plan on keeping your Fiero for ever and or you put lots of miles on it.  You will save $ in the long run, by spending a little more now and less later.  Of course this is just my opinion.<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||12
Z||000002||Jim's87GT||03-15-2000||05:05 PM||||RE: WTT3<BR>Thanks for the observation.  Surly you remember "My Mother The Car" on TV.  Well my car is more like "MY Confused Nephew".  I also appreciate the 'imho' note, being new to forums I hadn't figured out until you used it that it means 'in my humble' etc.<BR>Thanks again for the information and the welcome||||reg||1
Z||000003||Eric||03-15-2000||09:45 PM||||Eric's 88 GT loves its K&N.||||reg||12
Z||000004||87GT||03-15-2000||10:50 PM||||Kyle's 87GT cant tell any difference from the old filter to the K&N filter.  I always heard there was a noticeable change but I couldnt tell.||||reg||1
Z||000005||william_thorniii||03-16-2000||11:02 AM||||Jim,<P>Yes I do remember "My Mother the Car".  For the record, there was a thread in the O/T section about some common abbreviations used on-line.  You should easily be able to find it since there have only been some 300 topics in that section.  <P>The fact is that an air filter does not yeild enough performance to make a difference using the "seat-of-the-pants-omometer" that most of us use.  For the most part, all that can be told is that the engine revs faster, but that does not mean that it is faster.  I guess if anyone were interested enough they could have one dynoed.  I imagine that by freeing up some extra air, that they would be condusive to a better breathing engine.  Perhaps one of the dyno guys on the list knows for sure... You guys know who you are.  Have you just dynoed a filter?  If so, what did it do for performance.  <P>My previous recomendation was for the savings if you were to drive the car extensively.  I tried to stay away from the performance gain subject.  I did this intentionally because most peoples opinions are just that... opinions.  Some people have backed up their opinions with real #'s and those are what actually tells true story.  <P>Have Fun,<P>William T. Thorn, III<BR>||||reg||14
